Each group row now shows its spread: the highest scaled value among its people minus the lowest. `bin/e2e` passes, including the test-data replay, and the test sees 40, 20 and 870 for the three groups.

The change is only in the front end, `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people.ts`. The server already sent each person's scaled value, so spread is worked out in the browser the same way as the group's strength, size and cohesion. I added:
- a `group-concept-spread` element on each group row;
- a `groupSpreads` computed signal;
- a line in the header comment describing spread.

People whose scaled value is "n/a" are left out. A group where nobody has a scaled value, including an empty group, shows "n/a"; the test doesn't cover that case.

